    "notes": "Anchored-path prefilter fix: required-byte prefilter now runs in snobol_search_exec_anchored, so failing anchored matches (Pattern::match) on subjects lacking the required literal reject in one O(n) scan instead of full VM backtracking (prefilter_miss C: 136 -> 25 ns; PHP ~166 us -> ~230 ns at 200 iters, ~90 ns JIT-warm). The portable snobol_memmem (non-glibc) was a naive O(n*m) memcmp loop; it now skips via memchr, keeping the prefilter O(n) on macOS/MSVC (literal_fail anchored: 5429 -> 55 ns). C probe match rows for the residue family are now anchored (snobol_search_exec_anchored), pairing honestly with PHP match() rows. PHP binding: searchAll batch path pre-sizes result arrays with match_count; searchSplit uses the persistent-state batch (batch_ex). Coupling guard checks per-scenario ns-per-iteration ratios (residue_repeat/residue_zero_width/prefilter_miss/zero_progress at 10x, alt_literals at 50x). pike_overflow 891 -> ~2600 ns is the anchored BREAKX semantic (intentionally unoptimized), not a regression.",
